2. c4 d5 3. exd5 ( 3. cxd5 cxd5 4. exd5 Nf6 ) 3... cxd5 4. cxd5 ( 4. d4 Nf6 ) 4... Nf6 { Wins the pawn on d5 back and develops with tempo. } 5. Nc3 Nxd5 { Takes back the pawn. The knight is well placed in the centre, where it attacks the knight on c3. } 6. Nf3 Nc6 { Develops and adds pressure on d4 and e5. } 7. Bb5 e6 { Supports the knight on d5 and prepares to develop the bishop. } 8. O-O Be7 { Gets ready to castle. } 9. d4 O-O { King safe. Black has a healthy position and nothing to worry about. The knight on d5 is strong, so aim at the pawns with ...Bd7 and ...Rc8. If White varies, castle and play ...Bd7. } *
